Two-level periodic 1D advection for the AMR CPU-vs-Metal godunov diff: the central
density bump triggers one level of refinement (level 4 -> 5), so the coarse
level-4 cells at the refinement boundary exercise zero_fine_fluxes (fluxes at
faces touching a refined cell are zeroed).  Periodic -> no boundary octs.
Compile: make NDIM=1 HYDRO=1 COMPILER=METAL

&RUN_PARAMS
hydro=.true.
ncontrol=10000
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=4
levelmax=5
ngridmax=4000
nexpand=1
boxlen=1.0
/

&INIT_PARAMS
nregion=2
region_type(1)='square'
region_type(2)='square'
x_center=0.5,0.5
length_x=1.0,0.2
d_region=1.0,2.0
u_region=1.0,1.0
p_region=1.0,1.0
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
tout=1.0
/

&HYDRO_PARAMS
gamma=1.4
courant_factor=0.8
slope_type=2
riemann='hllc'
/

&REFINE_PARAMS
err_grad_d=0.05
interpol_type=1
/
